div.verse:
There are therefore three  
          Δογματα κυριου, Constitutions of the Lord. things ordained by the Lord; the hope of life;  
          Viz. faith and Charity. See before. the beginning and the completion of it.

Wherefore consider the works of the evil way.  
          Heb. x. 25. Do not withdraw yourselves from others, as if you were already justified; but coming altogether into one place, inquire what is agreeable to and profitable for the beloved of God. For the Scripture saith;  
          Vid. Gr. Clem. Alex. Isa. v., 21. Wo unto them that are wise in their own eyes, and prudent in their sight.

And again the prophet adds;  
          Ps. cxviii. 22. The stone which the builders refused has become the head of the corner. And again he saith;  
          V. 24. Clem. Alex. Strom. v. This is the great and wonderful day which the Lord hath made.  
          This is not in the Old Latin Version.  I write these things the more plainly to you that ye may understand:  
          Vid. Ed. Ox., p. 29, a. περιψημα της αγαπης υμων. For indeed I could be content even to die for your sakes.

Now what the spiritual meaning of this is, learn;  
          Vid. Cot. An. Marg. ex Clem. Alex. It is as if it had been said, Put your trust in Jesus, who shall be manifested to you in the flesh. For man is the earth which suffers: forasmuch as out of the  
          προσωπου. substance of the earth Adam was formed.

For thus the Scripture saith concerning us,  
          As he saith to the Son. where it introduceth the Father speaking to the Son;  
          Gen. i. 26. &c. Let us make man after our likeness and similitude; and let them have dominion over the beasts of the earth, and over the fowls of the air, and the fish of the sea.

The Lord saith;  
          Isa, xliii. 18, 19, &c. Behold I will make the last as the first. Wherefore the prophet thus spake,  
          Heb. iii. Enter into the land flowing with milk and honey, and have dominion over it.

But they have transgressed his commands, because the evil  
          Angel. one hath deceived them. For thus God bespeaks them;  
          Jer. iv. 3, 4. Thus saith the Lord your God (Here I find the new law) Sow not among thorns; but circumcise yourselves to the Lord your God. And what doth he mean by this saying? Hearken unto your Lord.

But because it might hereafter be said, that Christ was the Son of David;  
          Comp. Vet. Lat. Interp. therefore David fearing and well knowing the errors of the wicked, saith;  
          Psalm cix. 3. the Lord saith unto my Lord, sit thou on my right hand until I make thine enemies thy footstool.

And in another prophecy Jacob speaketh more clearly to his son Joseph saying;  
          Gen. xlviii. Behold the Lord hath not deprived me of seeing thy face, bring me thy sons that I may bless them. And he brought unto his father  
          Vid. Lat. Interp. Vet. Manasseh and Ephraim, desiring that he should bless Manasseh, because he was the elder.

And again the prophet saith;  
          Isaiah xlix. 6. Behold, I have set thee for a light unto the Gentiles, to be  
          For salvation unto. the saviour of all the ends of the earth, saith the Lord the God who hath redeemed thee.
